  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 63ecea1c26cf3bb4d9fad8c63b2e8ca7, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CombinedLoadingManager
  progressFill: {fileID: 1257370483}
  percentageText: {fileID: 1939662047}
  tipText: {fileID: 1472859294}
  skipHint: {fileID: 938830224}
  immediateScene: PlayerProfile
  preloadScene: 3_Kingdom1
  minLoadingTime: 10
  skipTime: 5
  tips:
  - "Go foods like rice and bread give your muscles glucose, the body\u2019s main
    fuel for running, thinking, and playing. "
  - Grow foods like fish, eggs, and beans are packed with protein, which the body
    breaks into amino acids to build muscles and repair cells.
  - 'Ultra-processed foods high in sugar can spike your blood sugar fast, then crash
    it, making you feel sleepy and cranky. '
  - "Too much salty processed food can strain your heart and blood vessels over time,
    so keep them as \u201Csometimes\u201D treats, not daily fuel. "
  - 'A plate with Go, Grow, and Glow foods is like a team: energy, building blocks,
    and cell protectors all working together to power your day. '
  - 'Vitamin C from glow foods like oranges and guava helps your body make collagen,
    keeping skin, gums, and wounds strong and quick to heal. '
  - "Some ultra-processed snacks are designed to be \u201Chyper tasty,\u201D so your
    brain wants more even when your tummy is already full. "
  - 'Many processed foods hide extra sugar using tricky names like corn syrup or
    maltose, so always check the ingredients list. '
  - 'Eating lots of ultra-processed foods over time is linked with a higher risk
    of obesity, diabetes, and heart disease. '
  - ong ingredient list with many hard-to-pronounce words? That is a clue your food
    is ultra-processed, not fresh.
  - 'The first 3 ingredients usually make up most of what you are actually eating. '
  - "Think of the first ingredient as the \u201Cboss\u201D of the food, and the next
    two as the \u201Csidekicks\u201D running the show. "
  tipInterval: 3
